meta {
  name: Send Notification
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/notify
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "text": "Hello from Bruno",
    "icon": "alert",
    "color": "#00FF00",
    "background": "#0A1A0A",
    "duration": 5000,
    "hold": false,
    "urgent": false,
    "stack": true
  }
}

docs {
  Sends a notification that interrupts app rotation.

  Notifications are displayed in a FIFO queue and auto-dismiss
  after their duration. App rotation resumes when the queue is empty.

  Parameters:
  - text: Notification text, max 127 chars (required). Takes a plain string, a
    colored one ({"text": "Build failed", "color": "#FF0000"}) or up to 8 colored
    segments ([{"t": "Build ", "c": "#FFFFFF"}, {"t": "failed", "c": "#FF0000"}]),
    concatenated in display order. A text that ends up empty - "", {"text": ""}
    or [] - is refused with HTTP 400 ("Missing text"). Accents are shown as their
    closest ASCII letter, and a color boundary placed after an accented character
    or a degree sign in the same string lands one glyph late for each of them
  - id: Unique ID, auto-generated "notif_<millis>" if omitted (optional)
  - icon: Icon name from /icons folder (optional)
  - color: Two roles - the color of any text sent without one of its own, and the
    color of the two separator lines unless background takes them over. Hex
    "#FF0000", RGB [255,0,0], or uint32 (default: white). Segments color the text
    only, so a fully segmented text still needs color set for the lines to match
  - background: Margin strip color above/below separators (default: black/none)
  - duration: Display duration in ms, 0 = hold indefinitely (default: 5000)
  - hold: If true, never auto-expires (default: false)
  - urgent: If true, jumps to front of queue (default: false)
  - stack: If true, queues after existing notifications. If false, clears queue first (default: true)
}
